{"summary": "Fixed the admin screen layout overflow. The admin screen was stacking title + 8-row listbox + 6-row form + feedback + back button vertically through the shared centred `body`, overflowing the 1100x750 window (title pushed off-screen at centre y=-9 and back button below the window).

Fixed by restructuring AdminScreen into a compact two-column layout using a dedicated `content` frame laid out with grid: title spanning both columns on top, question list in the left column (height 10, width 44), add/edit form (with all fields: prompt, correct value, kind, choices, plus Save and Delete buttons) in the right column, feedback and Back-to-Menu button at the bottom. This keeps the full form within the 1100x750 minimum size.

Re-verified: compile OK (36 files), full pytest suite passes (30 tests), no regressions."}
